{"record": "end", "run_id": "20261113T062726Z_dev-04_flat_1566", "reason": "answered", "detail": "", "answer": {"answer": "For the 4b on-shell cascade, the fixed-r slices show the AMS-02 antiproton limits approaching or intersecting the GCE-preferred regions at the smaller ratios, r = 0.2–0.4. At the larger ratios shown (up to r = 1.0, from the r = 0.2–1.0 panels), the antiproton limits stay above the GCE-preferred regions, so they do not constrain them. The paper notes that the strength of the antiproton bounds depends on the cascade spectra and the adopted cosmic-ray propagation model (BIG). It states this from the text describing the figure, and I could not view the figure panels themselves.", "found": true, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "6.3"}]}, "turns": 6, "seconds": 16.782, "tool_calls": 5, "tool_result_chars": 450322, "input_tokens": 14, "output_tokens": 685, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 67555, "cache_read_input_tokens": 650569, "parser_versions": ["4"], "response_models": ["claude-sonnet-5-5"], "ended_at": "2026-11-13T06:27:44+00:00"}
